module

/-
The One Piece

`K = ℚ(√−5)`.

Report `qsqrt5-rep-s1`: "ℚ(√−5) is the imaginary quadratic field of discriminant −20.
Its ring of integers is ℤ[√−5], with unit group {±1}. The ideal class group is cyclic of
order 2, generated by the class of 𝔭₂ = (2, 1+√−5)."

This formalizes what the field is. "What the Pit is made of," and whether
Portal / Pit / THE THING are the same, is her open question — not answered, not adjudicated.
The report (§7) says the same: those questions "are untouched by the theorems in §1–§5."
The theorems stop at the arithmetic.
-/

